<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maseru</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1869">1869</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maseru is the capital and largest city of Lesotho, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caledon-river">Caledon River</a> at the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>. It was founded in 1869 as a British police camp after Basutoland became a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>, and became the colonial capital. It remained the capital at independence in 1966.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maseru.jpg" alt="Maseru" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lschefa · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maseru_City_CBD.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
